            <ArticleTitle>Caring for the terminally ill adolescent.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>255-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Terminally ill adolescents, a heterogeneous group, face unique problems in coming to terms with the prospect of death and dying. In parallel, the psychosocial sequelae of a terminal illness in the adolescent, and their effects on the family and health professionals, present unique challenges for management. Using a developmental framework, we examine issues surrounding the care of dying adolescents and present strategies for their management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
